 "id": "economy",
 "kind": "rules",
 "note": "⚠️ SNG-300 (Erik: 'I want the value and money economy implemented'). PROMOTED FROM po/staged_content — this is the first economy content that is LIVE rather than drafted, and it is what `priceShift` has been waiting for. It supplies three things: the worth bands items now carry, the currencies a purse holds, and the per-region need/scarcity that turns a band into a price.",
 "worthBands": {
  "trivial": 1,
  "useful": 4,
  "valuable": 15,
  "precious": 50,
  "irreplaceable": {
   "value": null,
   "note": "not for sale — narrative only, and the engine should refuse a price"
  }
 },
 "priceModel": {
  "formula": "price = worthBands[item.worth] × need × scarcity",
  "need": {
   "none": 0.0,
   "little": 0.3,
   "ordinary": 1.0,
   "high": 2.0
  },
  "scarcity": {
   "abundant": 0.5,
   "ordinary": 1.0,
   "scarce": 1.8,
   "absent": 2.5
  },
  "rule": "⚠️ NEED DOMINATES AND `none` IS A HARD ZERO — Erik's correction. If a place does not want a thing, scarcity is irrelevant: nobody bids on what nobody uses. Scarcity only MODULATES an existing need, it never creates one. A one-axis model priced engine parts high in the Quickwood because they are rare there; they are rare there because nobody wants them.",
  "_bargainDoesNotBank_20260823": "⛔ ERIK'S CLARIFICATION, 2026-08-23. \"Not banking the deal\" means A BARGAIN NEVER PERMANENTLY CHANGES WHAT A THING IS WORTH — it does NOT mean the engine has no standard pricing. ⚠️ THE ENGINE KNOWS THE STANDARD PRICE AND MUST: `worthBands[item.worth] × need × scarcity` is the honest number the GM quotes, and it is the SAME number the next time anyone asks. A bargain moves what THIS deal settles at and nothing else. ⛔ VERIFIED AT RUNTIME 2026-08-23: standard price 4 before a won bargain, 3.98 settled, 4 again after — `item.worth`, region `need` and `scarcity` all untouched. ⚠️ THE FAILURE THIS FORBIDS: a haggler who talks a merchant down and thereby REPRICES grain for the region. A bargain is a conversation, not an economic event."
 },
